1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,780
Virginia had to pay a lottery crew twenty-seven fucking million dollars.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:12,200
This is part two, and in nineteen ninety-two, an Australian fund bought over five million tickets, almost every combo.

3
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,480
And yeah, they hit the jackpot, a state record.

4
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:19,960
But the state was pissed, 'cause the rule said tickets had to come from a licensed store.

5
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:24,400
And these guys? They had millions printed in bulk, like a damn print shop.

6
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:26,840
Double-tap if you'd have taken the money and run.

7
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:32,300
So Virginia investigated for three weeks. Nobody could prove a single broken rule.

8
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:35,920
So they paid one point three million a year, for twenty years.

9
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,660
That's twenty normal salaries, every year, for doing math.

10
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,320
Send this to whoever says the house always wins.

11
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:46,500
Then Virginia rushed in rules against bulk buying. Problem solved, right?

12
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:50,820
Hell no, because thirty-one years later, a group did it again in Texas.

13
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:54,040
Follow, 'cause the Texas part is even crazier.

14
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:57,480
They bought nearly every combo and won ninety-five million.

15
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:01,180
And the result? Texas shut down its whole lottery commission.

16
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,600
Genius or greedy? One word.

